/P 121 0 R
/E (The laws, regulations, and organizations that control the issuing, trading and oversight of financial instruments like bonds, shares, and debentures are together referred to as securities regulation. The regulatory environment in Bangladesh has changed to provide transparency, investment protection and accountability. The Bangladesh Securities and Exchange Commission \(BSEC\) which is known as the regulatory body, controls and monitors capital market. In addition to BSEC, Dhaka Stock Exchange \(DSE\) and Chittagong Stock Exchange \(CSE\) play important roles in the management of trading activities.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
