/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 122 0 R
/T ( Methodology of The Paper: The study primarily relies on secondary data. Information has been collected from textbooks, scholarly articles, annual reports, official publications, and reliable online sources related to the securities market of Bangladesh. Key legal instruments including the Securities Act and the Securities and Exchange Commission Act, along with other regulatory rules and guidelines, have been reviewed for analysis. Relevant information from the DSE and the CSE has also been included. The study explains the existing regulatory framework and evaluates its impact on the capital market based on available literature and data.)
/E ( Methodology of The Paper: The study primarily relies on secondary data. Information has been collected from textbooks, scholarly articles, annual reports, official publications, and reliable online sources related to the securities market of Bangladesh. Key legal instruments including the Securities Act and the Securities and Exchange Commission Act, along with other regulatory rules and guidelines, have been reviewed for analysis. Relevant information from the DSE and the CSE has also been included. The study explains the existing regulatory framework and evaluates its impact on the capital market based on available literature and data.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
