239 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (The securities market refers to the organized system where financial instruments such as shares, bonds, debentures and mutual funds are issued and traded. It plays a significant role in the country's financial system. It provides the companies and government a platform where long-term funds are raised and invested. The methods used to raise the money include private placements, right issues, and Initial Public Offering \(IPO\). It contributes to economic growth by channeling savings into productive investments.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
240 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (Components of the Securities Market:)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
241 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (The securities market in Bangladesh is divided into two sections. The first one is primary market and the other is secondary market. These two segments form the foundation of the capital market. They perform complementary functions in the process of capital mobilization and investment.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
242 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (It is the section of the securities market where new securities are issued for the first time. It is the initial platform where the new securities are issued. This market is used for raising long-term funds directly from the investors. The funds are raised through Initial Public Offerings \(IPO\), right issues and private placements. It promotes economic progress, business growth, financing infrastructure and long-term development initiatives.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
243 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (The secondary market is the segment which facilitates the trading of securities that have been issued in the primary market. It provides the investors a platform for trading securities freely. Liquidity and effective price discovery can be ensured by it. A well-organized secondary market strengthens investor confidence and encourages more market participation. In our country,the operations of both markets are carried out under the regulatory oversight of the Bangladesh Securities and Exchange Commission \(BSEC\) which ensures orderly market conduct, transparency and fairness.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
