/P 124 0 R
/T (Bangladesh Securities and Exchange Commission \(BSEC\): Bangladesh Securities and Exchange Commission \(BSEC\) was established as the regulator of the country's capital market under the provision of Bangladesh  Securities and Exchange Commission Act on 8th June, 1993. The purpose of the commission is to protect the interest of  the investors, develop the securities market, form policies,  supervise, licensing of the market participants, enforce the securities laws, prevent fraud and maintain transparency. It  consists of the Chairman and four Commissioners who are  appointed for full time by the Government. The Chairman acts as the Chief Executive of the Commission. The commission is a statutory body and it is attached to the Ministry of Finance. It is an 'A' category member of the International Organization of Securities Commissions \(IOSCO\)since 22 December 2013.)
/E (Bangladesh Securities and Exchange Commission \(BSEC\): Bangladesh Securities and Exchange Commission \(BSEC\) was established as the regulator of the country's capital market under the provision of Bangladesh  Securities and Exchange Commission Act on 8th June, 1993. The purpose of the commission is to protect the interest of  the investors, develop the securities market, form policies,  supervise, licensing of the market participants, enforce the securities laws, prevent fraud and maintain transparency. It  consists of the Chairman and four Commissioners who are  appointed for full time by the Government. The Chairman acts as the Chief Executive of the Commission. The commission is a statutory body and it is attached to the Ministry of Finance. It is an 'A' category member of the International Organization of Securities Commissions \(IOSCO\)since 22 December 2013.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
