/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (In Bangladesh, detailed rules on this issue were formulated through Margin Rules, 1999. These rules made written agreements mandatory for operating margin accounts and provided for maintaining equity at least 150%. If equity fell to 125%, the broker could sell shares. In addition, limits on single client and single security exposure were set and penalties were also provided for breaking the law. As a result, Margin Rules, 1999 served as a complete margin regulatory framework.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
