349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (Demutualization is a legal process to transform a stock exchange from a non-profit cooperative-based organization into a profitable and transparent public limited company. The main objective of this scheme, enacted under the Exchange Demutualization Act, 2013, is to completely separate the rights to trade shares \(TREC\) from the ownership of the exchange to reduce conflicts of interest while improving governance. A provision has been made to have 7 independent directors to ensure majority in the board of directors, which enhances transparency and good governance. In addition, 60% of the shares of the exchange have been reserved for strategic investors and the general public. The main objective of this scheme is to modernize the capital market, achieve international standards and protect the interests of investors.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
