<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (2. Corporate Governance: Companies must maintain independent directors, audit committees, transparent financial reporting, and ethical business practices in accordance with The Corporate Governance Guidelines of BSEC \(2006, revised 2012\). To ensure transparency and accountability in their operations, listed companies must follow the rules of corporate governance. But, unfortunately, governance in many companies has been reduced to formality and there exists untimely disclosures, poor audit committees. So, they must obtain a compliance certificate from an independent professional such as a Chartered Accountant or Cost and Management Accountant and disclose the certificate in their annual report.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [13 14]
>>
endobj
379 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (3. Market Efficiency and Transparency: BSEC asked stock exchanges to develop a unified web platform to update Consolidated Customers' Accounts \(CCA\) status daily after the trading close. It has also pushed for full automation of trade and settlement through the Central Depository Bangladesh Limited \(CDBL\). Moreover, the Financial Reporting Council \(FRC\) has improved auditing standards, reducing the use of false financial statements. It is to mention that penalties against non conformance are not so common and this discourages investor confidence, particularly institutional and foreign investors.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [15 16]
>>
endobj
